detail(1,'The development command starts the API host and frontend.<br><br>Default dev:web builds complete bundles and serves them with Vite preview.<br><br>dev:hmr is the separate HMR mode.', '"dev:web": "node scripts/dev-web.mjs"\n"dev:hmr": "concurrently ..."\n"dev:web:hmr": "vite"\n\n// server/index.ts\nconst app = await createApp();\napp.listen(port, "127.0.0.1");','package.json + server/index.ts · abbreviated excerpts','Startup establishes two local processes. The normal frontend command waits for a matching backend and serves completed bundles, with rebuild-and-reload behavior.','The separate hot-module command runs Vite directly. Do not describe the default development command as ordinary on-demand HMR. This distinction matters when diagnosing startup or stale frontend behavior.', ['package.json','scripts/dev-web.mjs','server/index.ts'],[0,1])
detail(2,'React starts a new run generation and AbortController.<br><br>It clears previous observations and validates the submitted body.<br><br>Live consent resets for each request.', 'const runGeneration =\n  generation.current.next();\nconst controller = new AbortController();\nsetState("running");\nsetFrames([]);\nsetConsent(false);\nsubmitted = bodySchema.parse(body);','src/App.tsx · selected ordered lines; other state updates omitted','React keeps run state separate from the saved learning checklist. A generation counter prevents an older run from overwriting the current view.','The submitted request is parsed with the shared schema. The current consent value goes into that request, while the checkbox is reset for the next one. An AbortController belongs to the active local request.', ['src/App.tsx','shared/contracts.ts'],[0])
detail(3,'The browser uses fetch with POST.<br><br>SSE observations are separated by blank lines.<br><br>A complete done event is required at stream end.', 'const response = await fetch(url, {\n  method: "POST",\n  headers: {\n    "Content-Type": "application/json"\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify(body), signal\n});\nconst reader = response.body.getReader();','src/stream.ts · excerpt; response checks omitted','The stream helper posts JSON and reads the response body incrementally. Vite forwards the API path to the local Express host.','The parser separates event blocks and JSON payloads. If the stream ends with a partial block or without done, it throws. A transport terminal still needs to be combined with the SDK result evidence.', ['src/stream.ts','vite.config.ts'],[0,1])
detail(4,'The host validates lesson-specific fields.<br><br>Live mode requires backend authentication and fresh consent.<br><br>Core Lessons 1–5 allow four active runs, with a 45-second host deadline.', 'if (active >= 4) {\n  res.status(429).json({\n    message: "All four exercise slots are busy."\n  });\n  return;\n}\nconst timer = setTimeout(\n  () => controller.abort(), 45000);','server/app.ts · selected excerpts from core lesson route','The route validates input before invoking a runner. It refuses a live call when consent or server authentication is absent, or live execution is disabled by host configuration.','This core route bounds concurrency and the run deadline. It also limits observed output. Later lesson routes have their own controls, so these numbers must not be presented as universal settings for all seventy-five labs.', ['server/app.ts'],[1])
detail(5,'Prepared mode emits authored observations.<br><br>Live mode calls the Agent SDK.<br><br>Prepared tool scenarios may still perform real local fixture actions.', 'await (config.runner ??\n  (body.mode === "prepared"\n    ? preparedRunner\n    : liveRunner))({\n      runId, lesson, body,\n      signal: controller.signal,\n      emit, store, tasks, permission\n    });','server/app.ts · runtime selection excerpt','Both paths use the same runner context, but their evidence sources differ. Prepared observations are scripted and do not measure the model.','Prepared tool lessons can still read or write allowed local fixture files. Live mode invokes query. A prepared error scenario does not force a live model to produce the same error.', ['server/app.ts','server/runtime.ts'],[1])
detail(6,'selectedOptions chooses model, tools and limits.<br><br>Lesson 1 defaults to one turn and a 0.05 USD SDK budget option.<br><br>The host supplies an owned working directory.', 'Object.assign(options, {\n  abortController,\n  settingSources: [],\n  strictMcpConfig: true,\n  cwd: ctx.store.root\n});\nconst run = query({\n  prompt: ctx.body.prompt, options\n});','server/runtime.ts · excerpt','The first lesson uses a bounded text-only configuration. The selected model comes from the host environment or its default. Do not confuse an SDK budget option with a universal guarantee about final billed cost.','The runtime sets its working directory, excludes implicit setting sources, and uses strict MCP configuration before calling query. Later tool lessons add permissions, hooks, and explicit MCP server definitions.', ['server/runtime.ts'],[1,2])
detail(7,'The async iterator yields SDK messages.<br><br>The host wraps them as SSE message frames.<br><br>Cancellation reaches the SDK AbortController; finally closes the query.', 'try {\n  for await (const event of run) {\n    ctx.emit("message", event);\n  }\n} finally {\n  run.close();\n  ctx.signal.removeEventListener(\n    "abort", abort);\n}','server/runtime.ts · excerpt; TypeScript cast omitted','The application consumes the query as an async iterable. It forwards SDK messages while they arrive, rather than waiting for one final JSON document.','The finally block closes the query and removes the abort listener. The host route also clears its timer, cancels unresolved permission decisions, releases the active slot, and ends the response. Failure and cancellation must not be displayed as a successful run.', ['server/runtime.ts','server/app.ts'],[1,2])
detail(8,'The evaluator requires completed transport evidence and a successful parent result.<br><br>Partial text does not establish completion.<br><br>The resulting check is saved separately from self-assessment.', 'const results = messages.filter(m =>\n  m.type === "result" &&\n  !m.parent_tool_use_id);\nconst terminal = results.at(-1);\nif (!terminal ||\n    terminal.subtype !== "success" ||\n    terminal.is_error !== false) {\n  return failure("A final successful parent result is required; partial text is not completion.");\n}','shared/contracts.ts · excerpt, reformatted','After the stream closes normally, the UI evaluates the collected evidence. It needs a final successful parent result and no operation error, along with the lesson-specific criteria.','Lesson one still leaves answer quality to manual review. Other lessons require matched tool calls, arguments, results, or file evidence. The check records observed conditions; it does not certify every claim in the generated answer.', ['shared/contracts.ts','src/App.tsx'],[0])
add('Tools, permissions and MCP',head('HOST CONTROL OVER TOOL OPERATIONS','Availability, approval and evidence are different')+'<div class="grid">'+card('tools-available','Which tools exist?','Configured tools and allowedTools<br>Built-in tool selection<br>Custom tools through MCP')+card('tools-permission','May this call run?','Hooks and canUseTool<br>Owned file targets<br>Correlated Allow / Deny response')+card('tools-evidence','What actually happened?','Matching call and result IDs<br>Handler name + arguments<br>File hashes or other host evidence')+'</div>',[('tools-available','Configured tool availability is one part of the policy. The runtime can also provide custom tools through createSdkMcpServer.'),('tools-permission','Permissions decide whether a particular operation may run. The interactive permission lesson correlates the decision with the active run and call, and restricts file targets.'),('tools-evidence','Then inspect evidence of the operation. A tool name appearing in text is not the same as a matched successful tool result or verified file change.')],['server/runtime.ts','server/app.ts','server/lab-store.ts','shared/contracts.ts'])
add('Learning state and execution state',head('WHERE STATE LIVES','Browser records, host files and SDK sessions')+'<div class="grid">'+card('state-browser','Browser-local learning','Theme and preferences<br>Notes and checkpoints<br>Knowledge and exercise checks')+card('state-host','Host-owned local data','Ignored .data/lab directory<br>Fixture files and lesson stores<br>AI Tutor saved-answer storage')+card('state-session','Session persistence varies','Some session registries are memory-only<br>Dedicated persistence lessons add stores<br>Inspect the selected runtime')+'</div><div class="banner"><p>This is a trusted local teaching host, not an authenticated multi-tenant cloud service.</p></div>',[('state-browser','The browser stores supported preferences, notes, and learning records locally. These are separate from SDK observations and do not automatically synchronize between devices.'),('state-host','The host maintains owned fixture files and lesson-specific data. Storage policy varies by feature, including saved AI Tutor answers.'),('state-session','Some session handles are memory-only and reset with the host. Dedicated persistence lessons add their own behavior. Do not assume that every query is durably stored by the learning platform.')],['src/course-state.ts','src/browser-preferences.ts','server/lab-store.ts','server/ai-tutor-store.ts','README.md'])
add('AI Tutor and milestone projects',head('LEARNING FEATURES AROUND THE CORE RUNTIME','Contextual support and cumulative application work')+'<div class="grid">'+card('tutor','AI Tutor','Prepared guidance or explicit live request<br>Lesson context and source snippets<br>Saved answer and provenance controls')+card('milestones','Three milestone starters','Study Coach<br>Agent Evaluation Studio<br>Agent Publishing Studio')+card('extensions','Specialized execution surfaces','MCP integrations and browser labs<br>Python SDK bridge<br>Editor extension and other adapters')+'</div>',[('tutor','The AI Tutor builds guidance from the current lesson context. Prepared guidance and live generation remain distinct, with their own request and save behavior.'),('milestones','Three runnable milestone starters support cumulative work: a Study Coach, an Agent Evaluation Studio, and an Agent Publishing Studio. The numbered stage prompts guide the student through implementation.'),('extensions','Specialized lessons add different execution surfaces, such as Python, editor integration, or browser automation. Each requires its own setup and evidence rather than inheriting success from the first query.')],['server/ai-tutor.ts','server/mini-projects.ts','README.md'])
